# §11.3 — the obfuscation toolchain is dev-only. `build/release/` is the whole release tree
# (regenerated from source by `npm run build`), and `build/sourcemaps/` is §8.4's
# 「sourcemap 上传到私密位置」 — it is deliberately NOT in the extension, so it must not be in git
# either, because a sourcemap in the repo is the unobfuscated source with a bow on it.
build/release/
build/sourcemaps/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# §8.4 / docs/DEPLOY.md — `supabase/config.toml` is the LOCAL copy you create from the committed
# `config.example.toml` (`cp supabase/config.example.toml supabase/config.toml`) when you run
# `supabase start`, and `supabase/.temp/` is the CLI's own scratch directory. The EXAMPLE is the
# reviewable artefact; the local copy is per-machine state. Neither has real secrets — secrets go
# in with `supabase secrets set`, never in this file — so this is hygiene, not a security fix.
supabase/config.toml
supabase/.temp/
